Playing around a bit with a wizard atm, I wonder for what purpose one
would want to write a spellbook. Obviously one can only write a
spellbook of an already known spell... but if I already know the spell,
I don't need the  spellbook, do I? (besides I usually already have the
spellbook, because I learned the spell from it) Do spellbooks have any
other use, than learning new spells? I even tend to throwing away my
spellbooks as soon, as I have learned the respective spell, because they
are heavy.

